course: dictionary
lesson: 2167
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Corporal is one of these. As a noun, a corporal is a soldier. As an adjective, it means to do with the body.
explain: «The tiny Napoleon idea grew from British cartoons that mocked him... and from his nickname "the little corporal" (a corporal is a low army rank), which was a friendly name, not a measurement.» The clue is army rank, so here corporal is a noun. Ask yourself: is this word naming a person, or describing something?
explain: Corporal is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in set phrases. In «corporal punishment», the word describes the punishment, and it means punishment that hurts the body, such as hitting.
fact: A corporal is a soldier with a low rank, above a private, who is in charge of a small group of soldiers.
fact: «Corporal Smith» uses corporal as a title, a bit like Mr or Mrs, for a soldier.
fact: Corporal (adjective) means to do with the body, and it is a formal word.
fact: «Corporal punishment» means punishing someone by hitting them. It used to happen in schools, but it is now banned in schools in the UK, Ireland, New Zealand, Canada and most of Australia.
fact: Napoleon's nickname «the little corporal» was a friendly name, not a measurement.
exercise: «The corporal led his small group of soldiers across the field.» What is a corporal? | A bird that sings at dawn | A king who rules a whole country | A large, heavy stone | *A soldier with a low rank who is in charge of a small group
exercise: Nadia reads «corporal punishment» in a history book. What does corporal mean in this phrase? | To do with the sky | To do with money | *To do with the body | To do with the sea
exercise: «Corporal Smith» is written at the top of the orders. What is corporal doing here? | Describing a long journey | *Acting as a title for a soldier | Naming a school subject | Naming a type of food
test: Which sentence uses corporal as an adjective? | «The corporal wore a red jacket.» | «The corporal waited by the gate.» | «The corporal led the patrol at dawn.» | *«Corporal punishment is now banned in many schools.»
test: In «the little corporal», what does corporal mean? | A very tall person | A type of cartoon | A measurement of height | *A low army rank, so the name was a friendly nickname
exam: Ella reads «The corporal saluted the captain» and then «corporal punishment». Which statement is right? | *In the first, corporal is a noun for a soldier; in the second, it is an adjective about the body | Corporal always means a loud shout | Both are nouns for a soldier | Both mean to do with the body
